Reason for this patch: FAST-LIO reads Livox scans only as CustomMsg (its PointCloud2 parsers are for Velodyne and Ouster layouts).
In AAS, /livox/lidar carries livox_ros_driver2's CustomMsg (xfer_format 1), from the Mid-360's driver on the drone and from livox_sim in simulation.
Upstream's CustomMsg input is half-ported ROS1 code: CMake looks for ROS1's livox_ros_driver, so in ROS2 the input is compiled out (and it has typos).
Changes:
- CMakeLists.txt: find livox_ros_driver2, REQUIRED (the build fails instead of dropping the input)
- preprocess.h, preprocess.cpp: livox_ros_driver2's CustomMsg instead of ROS1's; avia_handler declared as defined (const reference); RCLCPP_DEBUG instead of ROS1's ROS_DEBUG
- spark_fast_lio.h, spark_fast_lio.cpp: typos that do not compile (livoxLidarCallback for livoxLiDARCallback, the guard LIVOXROS_DRIVER_FOUND for LIVOX_ROS_DRIVER_FOUND,
  imu_buffer for imu_buffer_, nanseconds() for nanoseconds()); the callback takes a const reference, as its body uses
- spark_fast_lio.cpp: subscribe to CustomMsg on "livox" (AAS: -r livox:=/livox/lidar) instead of "lidar" (ROS2's FastDDS cannot have two message types on one topic in one node)
- preprocess.cpp (avia_handler): the parentheses of the original hku-mars/FAST_LIO, so that points closer than preprocess.blind are dropped

